From 540a37ec54eab7e8f69a35d7f3a872dbfe637ca9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:50:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] feat(web): build the dashboard and chat UI without
 Vite's native tools

Vite 7 cannot run where esbuild (Go) and Rollup 4 (a Rust parser) have no
prebuilt binaries, and neither can be built on hosts without Go/Rust
(e.g. PowerPC Macs), so -DFORGE_BUILD_DASHBOARD=ON was unusable there.

tools/web-build/build.mjs produces the same dist/ layout from web/ and
web-chat/ in plain JavaScript: Rollup 3 (+ node-resolve, commonjs),
@vue/compiler-sfc for <script setup lang="ts"> / <style scoped>,
TypeScript's transpileModule for type stripping, terser, and a small CSS
collector that copies url() assets (the KaTeX fonts). Its dependencies
are pinned in its own package-lock.json at the frontends' runtime
versions; TypeScript is optional and may come from NODE_PATH.

CMake: -DFORGE_DASHBOARD_BUILDER=portable selects it (default: vite, as
before). FORGE_NPM_CACHE and FORGE_NPM_CI_ARGS let packagers install from
a pre-filled cache offline (e.g. "--offline;--omit=optional"), for both
builders.

Checked on x86-64 against a Vite build of the same sources: bundle sizes
within 2% (Vite: 678/460 KB JS, portable: 667/457 KB), and the frontends'
own jsdom tests pass on the portable output (web: bundle + theme;
web-chat: test-ui-bundle, 73 checks). An offline npm ci from the 58
locked tarballs with TypeScript 6.0.2 from NODE_PATH gives byte-identical
output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
